/Remote Work Resources Office of the Provost Baylor Round Table Ignite Great Colleges to Work For® Survey Baylor Human Resources Careers at Baylor Consistently ranked as one of the nation’s “Great Colleges to Work For” by the Chronicle of Higher Education , Baylor is a rewarding place to build a career. With a student population of more than 20,000, pursuing over 250 degree programs, in world-class facilities, spread over a beautiful 1,000-acre campus located on the Brazos River, Baylor is like a small city—with full and part-time opportunities utilizing a wide variety of skills. Why Baylor? Explore Employment Opportunities To explore career options, learn how to apply, and view current positions—this is the place to start. View our employment notices Faculty Teaching, research & scholarship opportunities View Faculty Positions Staff Administrative, professional, IT, technical, clerical & service positions View Staff Positions Other Campus Employment Contract, part-time, temporary, student jobs & graduate assistantships Learn More Summer Camp Employment Athletics/recreation, sports management, music, ministry and more. Learn More Baylor Advantages More Advantages Baylor employees enjoy a wide range of advantages, benefits, perks and privileges not often available at most universities. Athletic Tickets Faculty, staff, and retirees are eligible for discounted or free admission to campus Athletic events. About Athletics Tickets Dining Discounts & Options There are several on-campus dining options and many offer discounts up to 50% off based on an employee's status. About Dining Options Free Parking Faculty and staff receive on-campus parking access at no charge. About Free Parking Recreation, Fitness & Nutrition Baylor has a free on-site fitness center, nutrition advisement, and recreational activities for Baylor faculty, staff, and their families. About Campus Recreation Mayborn Museum The Mayborn Museum features natural science and cultural history focusing on Central Texas while offering multiple fun discovery rooms that encourage hands-on learning. About The Mayborn Campus Events Throughout the year, Baylor hosts many exciting campus-wide events such as Dr Pepper Hour, Diadeloso, Staff Forums, and many more to enjoy. About Campus Events Adoption Assistance As part of Baylor's commitment to a caring Christian community, the Adoption Assistance Program helps families going through the adoption process. About Adoption Assistance Personal Technology Discounts Baylor faculty and staff have access to special discounts on computers, printers, and other technology accessories. About Technology Discounts About Baylor The values, vision, campus & culture that set Baylor apart Wellbeing Resources & support for every dimension of your personal health Employee & Family Resources Job search, living, legal & financial services for spouse & family Veterans Academic resources, career development & financial support Accommodation Requests Information, policies, eligibility & accommodations About Waco Education is big here. Quality of life is valued here. People are welcoming here. And dollars go further here, with a cost of living well below the national average. Learn More About Waco Employment Notices Notice of Non-Discrimination Baylor University, a private not-for-profit university affiliated with the Baptist General Convention of Texas, is committed to compliance with all applicable anti-discrimination laws, including those regarding age, race, color, sex, national origin, military service, genetic information, and disability. Baylor complies with statutory Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity requirements. Baylor's full official Notice of Non-Discrimination may be read online. Baylor University's Full Notice of Non-Discrimination Need Accommodation to Apply? In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act Amendments Act (ADAAA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Baylor University, please call 254-710-2000 or e-mail askHR@baylor.edu . Request Accommodations Clery Notifications Baylor University is required by federal law to publish an Annual Fire Safety and Security Report. This report includes institutional policies, procedures and programs concerning safety and security. Some of the areas addressed within the report include crime prevention, fire safety, and Baylor’s response to emergency situations and sexual offenses. Three years of statistics for certain types of crimes that were reported to have occurred on campus, in or on off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by the school and on public property within or immediately adjacent to the campus are also included. This report is available online at https://www.baylor.edu/annualcleryreport/ . You may also request a paper copy from Baylor Department of Public Safety (254-710-2211). Clery Compliance Baylor Human Resources Putting People First. Clifton Robinson Tower | Suite 200 700 S University Parks Dr Waco, TX 76706 One Bear Place #97053 Waco, TX 76798 askhr@baylor.edu 254-710-2000 Ask HR About Jobs Disclosures Visit Policies Human Resources Careers & Opportunities About Careers & Opportunities Back Research & Learn Back Staff Job Descriptions whyBaylor Apply & Interview Back Faculty Application Process Staff Application Process Veteran Resources for Interviewing New Faculty and Staff Back Welcome & Orientation Back Living in Waco Steps for New Faculty Back New Faculty Orientation Steps for New Staff New Employee Forms Back Completing Your I-9 Back FAQs for Completing Your I-9 Employment Forms by State Transition & Exit Back Exiting Faculty Exiting Staff Contingent Workers (Auxiliaries) Other Campus Employment Back Summer Camp Employment Visa Sponsorship and Support Back Hiring and Support of International Scholars Next Steps for International Scholars Additional Resources Benefits & Advantages Back My Benefits Back Veteran Resources Baylor Wellbeing Enrol