Remote Work Resources Office of the Provost Baylor Round Table Ignite Great Colleges to Work For® Survey Human Resources Careers & Opportunities Research & Learn Research & Learn Staff Job Descriptions whyBaylor Apply & Interview New Faculty and Staff Transition & Exit Contingent Workers (Auxiliaries) Other Campus Employment Visa Sponsorship and Support Additional Resources Research & Learn We are excited and thankful that you have chosen to include Baylor in your career search! This page provides a wealth of information and links for you to research and learn about Baylor University and all we have to offer! Working at Baylor Consistently ranked as a \"Great College to Work For\" by the Chronicle of Higher Education, we offer our employees so much more than just a job!  As part of the Baylor family, employees not only receive a comprehensive benefits package that includes medical and dental insurance, generous time off, and fantastic automatic retirement contributions, they also get to experience Baylor. Not only is Baylor highly rated by the Chronicle, we are also highly rated by our faculty and staff. Take a look at our reviews on Glassdoor: From free admission to various athletic events, access to wonderful libraries, museums, and recreational facilities, and tuition remission for faculty and staff and their dependents, it is no wonder Baylor employees consistently rank the University as a great place to build a career! Benefits Summary Our Compensation Philosophy About Baylor Founded in 1845 by the Republic of Texas, Baylor is a private Christian university and a nationally ranked research institution.  Our more than 3,000 mission-focused faculty and staff create a transformative educational environment and experience for our nearly 17,000 undergraduate and graduate students. Awards and Rankings Learn and Grow Our employees are encouraged to continue to grow and learn new skills.  In addition to our tuition remission benefit, we provide a broad range of learning opportunities for our staff members. Career Learning Courses Living the Baylor Mission Our mission defines who we are as an institution, and guides us in our every action. We take the words in our mission statement seriously as Baylor strives to be a leader in higher education. Mission Statement Explore More Baylor Research Focus Christian Commitment Strategic Plan and Goals Baylor Campus Map Living in Waco Cost of Living Calculator Baylor Human Resources Putting People First. Clifton Robinson Tower | Suite 200 700 S University Parks Dr Waco, TX 76706 One Bear Place #97053 Waco, TX 76798 askhr@baylor.edu 254-710-2000 Ask HR About Jobs Disclosures Visit Policies Human Resources Careers & Opportunities Research & Learn About Careers & Opportunities Back Research & Learn Back Staff Job Descriptions whyBaylor Apply & Interview Back Faculty Application Process Staff Application Process Veteran Resources for Interviewing New Faculty and Staff Back Welcome & Orientation Back Living in Waco Steps for New Faculty Back New Faculty Orientation Steps for New Staff New Employee Forms Back Completing Your I-9 Back FAQs for Completing Your I-9 Employment Forms by State Transition & Exit Back Exiting Faculty Exiting Staff Contingent Workers (Auxiliaries) Other Campus Employment Back Summer Camp Employment Visa Sponsorship and Support Back Hiring and Support of International Scholars Next Steps for International Scholars Additional Resources Benefits & Advantages Back My Benefits Back Veteran Resources Baylor Wellbeing Enrollment Back Benefitfocus Information Benefitfocus Login 2026 Benefits Guide What's New for 2026 Retirement Back Investing in Your Retirement Back Baylor 457(b) Plan Baylor Retirement Plan - 403(b) Importance of Retirement Planning TIAA Updates - New Features Preparing for Your Retirement Back Retiree Insurance Details Back Health Reimbursement Account (HRA) Medicare Basic Information Retiring Process Checklist Enjoying Your Retirement Back My Retiree Benefits Te