      "title": "Staff Application Process",
      "description": "Staff Application Process | Human Resources | Baylor University Skip to main content Skip to main navigation Open Mobile Navigation Human Resources About Careers & Opportunities Research & Learn Staff Job Descriptions whyBaylor Apply & Interview Faculty Application Process Staff Application Process Veteran Resources for Interviewing New Faculty and Staff Welcome & Orientation Steps for New Faculty Steps for New Staff New Employee Forms Employment Forms by State Transition & Exit Exiting Faculty Exiting Staff Contingent Workers (Auxiliaries) Other Campus Employment Summer Camp Employment Visa Sponsorship and Support Hiring and Support of International Scholars Next Steps for International Scholars Additional Resources Benefits & Advantages My Benefits Veteran Resources Baylor Wellbeing Enrollment Benefitfocus Information Benefitfocus Login 2026 Benefits Guide What's New for 2026 Retirement Investing in Your Retirement Preparing for Your Retirement Enjoying Your Retirement Retiree Advantages Retiree Benefits Overview Compensation Compensation Philosophy and Resources Total Compensation Statement Fair Labor Standards Act (FLSA) Merit Insurance Offerings Medical Insurance Plans Prescription Drug Plan Dental Insurance Plan Vision Insurance Plan Employer Provided Insurances Retiree Insurance Details Continuation of Insurance Coverage Voluntary Supplemental Insurances Pet Insurance Employee Recognition Tuition Remission Time Off & Leave Policies Family and Medical Leave Act (FMLA) Maternity and Primary Caregiver Leave Paid Caregiver Leave Paid Parental Leave Timecards During University Closures Employee Caregiver & Family Resources Adoption Assistance Program Crisis Resources Care.com Spousal Employment Assistance Educational Assistance Expectant & New Parents Progyny Surviving Spouse Benefits Baylor Advantages Athletic Tickets Baby Bear Program Baylor Bookstore Baylor Club at McLane Stadium Baylor Theatre Baylor Wellbeing BearStand Campus Dining Offerings Campus Recreation Credit Union Emotional Wellbeing Solutions Game Room Health Center Martin Museum of Art Massage Therapy Mayborn Museum Complex Parking Personal Technology Purchases Personal Cell Phone Discounts Real Appeal School of Music University Libraries Waco Perks Benefit Forms Benefitfocus Login Manage & Lead Getting Started Core Commitments Leadership Commitments Management Toolkits & Guides Faculty Performance Process How to Approve Timecards in Ignite Managing Performance Year-Round One on One Resources Performance Helpers Performance Improvement Plan Performance Review Process - Manager Guide Recruiting and Hiring Staff Second-Level Managers: What are they and what do they do? Staff Performance Review Process Baylor Workforce Structure Additional Resources Sabbaticals, Research Leaves, and Grants System Instructions & Access Questions Tuition & Teaching Learn & Grow Available Course Listings Chronological Available Course Listings Grow@BU Grow@BU Participant Spotlights Lead@BU Lead@BU Initiative Completions Career Tools Career Conversations Individual Development Plan Faculty Development Educational Assistance Tuition Remission Tuition Reimbursement Resources & Reporting Engage with HR Contacts askHR HRC - Human Resources Consultants Human Capital Management (HCM) Specialists Talent Advising Contact List Student Employment Faculty Senate and Staff Council Baylor Organizational Chart Employee Resource Groups - ERGs Asian American & Pacific Islander Faculty & Staff Association (AAPIFSA) Black Faculty & Staff Association (BFSA) Disability Faculty and Staff Association (DFSA) Jewish Faculty & Staff Association (JFSA) Latinx Faculty & Staff Association (LFSA) Military-Connected Faculty & Staff Association (MCFSA) Policies & Postings Fraud alert: Unemployment Claims and Identity Theft Required Annual Notices State Employment Law Postings Giving How to Report Concerns Additional Employee Resources Emotional Wellbeing Solutions (EWS) Christian Conciliation Hybrid/Remote Work Resources Office of the Provost Baylor Round Table Ignite Great Colleges to Work For® Survey Human Resources Careers & Opportunities Apply & Interview Staff Application Process Research & Learn Apply & Interview Faculty Application Process Staff Application Process Veteran Resources for Interviewing New Faculty and Staff Transition & Exit Contingent Workers (Auxiliaries) Other Campus Employment Visa Sponsorship and Support Additional Resources Staff Application Process Frequently Asked Questions If you have questions about our application process, you are not alone! We have a designated team of Talent Advisors ready to support you through your application process. View our Talent Advising contact list to reach out to the Advisor associated with the position that you are applying for. They are able to assist with many questions, including: Why does Baylor ask about my religion on the application? What does “relevant experience” mean? To whom should I address my cover letter? Steps to Apply for Staff Positions Start your Baylor career search by visiting baylor.edu/jobs . Scroll and view all open staff positions by clicking on the \"Staff\" button. Refine your search by position title, department information, or by using keywords. Click on the job title to learn more about a position. Click on the \"Apply for this Job\" at the top of the job posting to submit an application. If you already have a user account, you will be asked to log into your account and submit your application. If this is your first time to apply at Baylor, you will need to create a user account.  When you click to apply to a position, you will be prompted to create an account.  You can also create an account from the main page by clicking on the \"Create an Account\" button on the left side of the page. Remember, you will also be asked to upload a resume and custom cover letter for each position to which apply! Once you have an account, you can check the status of the application, edit your profile, and apply for new jobs. For technical assistance specifically with our jobs page, please email Human_Resources@baylor.edu . Application Review and Selection Process Once we receive your application, a Talent Advisor in Human Resources will review it to determine if all required qualifications are met. If the application meets the stated minimum qualifications, it will be sent to the hiring department for further consideration. If the hiring department decides to request an interview, you will be contacted by a representative from either Human Resources or the hiring department to schedule a time. The typical selection process can take 8 to 10 weeks to complete. If you are a finalist for the position, you will receive a request for information to complete a background check and a minimum of three professional references. Please note that a request for references and background check does not constitute a job offer, as references and checks are conducted on most finalists. All applicants will be notified via email once a final decision is made. If you are selected to receive a job offer, you will be contacted directly by a Talent Advisor. Baylor Human Resources Putting People First. Clifton Robinson Tower | Suite 200 700 S University Parks Dr Waco, TX 76706 One Bear Place #97053 Waco, TX 76798 askhr@baylor.edu 254-710-2000 Ask HR About Jobs Disclosures Visit Policies Human Resources Careers & Opportunities Apply & Interview Staff Application Process About Careers & Opportunities Back Research & Learn Back Staff Job Descriptions whyBaylor Apply & Interview Back Faculty Application Process Staff Application Process Veteran Resources for Interviewing New Faculty and Staff Back Welcome & Orientation Back Living in Waco Steps for New Faculty Back New Faculty Orientation Steps for New Staff New Employee Forms Back Completing Your I-9 Back FAQs for Completing Your I-9 Employment Forms by State Transition & Exit Back Exiting Faculty Exiting Staff Contin