brid/Remote Work Resources Office of the Provost Baylor Round Table Ignite Great Colleges to Work For® Survey New Faculty and Staff Welcome to Baylor. Congratulations on your new position, and welcome to the Baylor Family. You are joining a world-class faculty and staff, a diverse and dedicated community with a strong commitment to faith, and an active, vibrant campus teeming with leading-edge facilities, championship athletics, and outstanding students. Before you step into your new Baylor role, there’s a lot to learn and do. Let’s get started … Explore New Employee Forms Getting Started To make your transition into your new job as smooth and easy as possible, we’ve mapped out your journey, step-by step. To see what lies ahead, view your itinerary. Welcome & Orientation We are excited you have chosen to build your career here. All new hires attend the new hire orientation named Called to BU. This is a critical first step in your success at Baylor. Welcome & Orientation Steps for New Faculty At Baylor, you are an important part of a world class faculty and staff dedicated to teaching and research, championship athletic programs, outstanding student involvement, and a diverse community with a strong commitment to faith. Steps for New Faculty Steps for New Staff At Baylor, you will find a world class faculty and staff dedicated to teaching and research, championship athletic programs, outstanding student involvement and a diverse community with a strong commitment to faith. Steps for New Staff Wellbeing Accommodation Requests Baylor Traditions About Waco Employee & Family Resources Baylor Human Resources Putting People First. Clifton Robinson Tower | Suite 200 700 S University Parks Dr Waco, TX 76706 One Bear Place #97053 Waco, TX 76798 askhr@baylor.edu 254-710-2000 Ask HR About Jobs Disclosures Visit Policies Human Resources Careers & Opportunities New Faculty and Staff About Careers & Opportunities Back Research & Learn Back Staff Job Descriptions whyBaylor Apply & 