brid/Remote Work Resources Office of the Provost Baylor Round Table Ignite Great Colleges to Work For® Survey Human Resources Careers & Opportunities New Faculty and Staff Welcome & Orientation Research & Learn Apply & Interview New Faculty and Staff Welcome & Orientation Living in Waco Steps for New Faculty Steps for New Staff New Employee Forms Employment Forms by State Transition & Exit Contingent Workers (Auxiliaries) Other Campus Employment Visa Sponsorship and Support Additional Resources Welcome & Orientation Congratulations and Welcome to Baylor! We are excited you have chosen to build your career at Baylor! All new staff hires attend the new hire orientation called Called to BU. This is a critical first step in your success at Baylor. Called to BU is hosted weekly in Clifton Robinson Tower and covers important topics such as Baylor's history and culture, compliance requirements, and a review of our outstanding benefits package. All local employees must attend in person on their scheduled date. If you are a remote employee and are not scheduled to be in Waco, virtual arrangements will be provided to you. This page is designed to help you connect with the many resources available to you as a new faculty or staff member. You can explore a campus map, take a virtual tour, begin to prepare for your first day with helpful links to information about onboarding and orientation, and much, much more! Baylor Orientation Guide Steps for New Faculty Steps for New Staff Find Your Way Around Campus Map Virtual Campus Tour Learn to Be a Bear Attend new hire orientation: Called to BU Baylor Traditions Senior Leadership at Baylor Get What You Need Human Resources Parking & IDs Dining Services Important Reading Policies Welcome to Waco Discover Waco Waco Culture Guide Wacoan - Waco's Magazine Family Resources Baylor Wellbeing Emotional Wellbeing Solutions (EWS) Dual Career Assistance Find a Church Find Childcare Find a House Family Benefits at Baylor Baylor Human Resources Pu