    "https://hr.web.baylor.edu/careers-opportunities/new-faculty-and-staff/steps-new-faculty": {
      "title": "Steps for New Faculty",
      "description": "Steps for New Faculty | Human Resources | Baylor University Skip to main content Skip to main navigation Open Mobile Navigation Human Resources About Careers & Opportunities Research & Learn Staff Job Descriptions whyBaylor Apply & Interview Faculty Application Process Staff Application Process Veteran Resources for Interviewing New Faculty and Staff Welcome & Orientation Steps for New Faculty Steps for New Staff New Employee Forms Employment Forms by State Transition & Exit Exiting Faculty Exiting Staff Contingent Workers (Auxiliaries) Other Campus Employment Summer Camp Employment Visa Sponsorship and Support Hiring and Support of International Scholars Next Steps for International Scholars Additional Resources Benefits & Advantages My Benefits Veteran Resources Baylor Wellbeing Enrollment Benefitfocus Information Benefitfocus Login 2026 Benefits Guide What's New for 2026 Retirement Investing in Your Retirement Preparing for Your Retirement Enjoying Your Retirement Retiree Advantages Retiree Benefits Overview Compensation Compensation Philosophy and Resources Total Compensation Statement Fair Labor Standards Act (FLSA) Merit Insurance Offerings Medical Insurance Plans Prescription Drug Plan Dental Insurance Plan Vision Insurance Plan Employer Provided Insurances Retiree Insurance Details Continuation of Insurance Coverage Voluntary Supplemental Insurances Pet Insurance Employee Recognition Tuition Remission Time Off & Leave Policies Family and Medical Leave Act (FMLA) Maternity and Primary Caregiver Leave Paid Caregiver Leave Paid Parental Leave Timecards During University Closures Employee Caregiver & Family Resources Adoption Assistance Program Crisis Resources Care.com Spousal Employment Assistance Educational Assistance Expectant & New Parents Progyny Surviving Spouse Benefits Baylor Advantages Athletic Tickets Baby Bear Program Baylor Bookstore Baylor Club at McLane Stadium Baylor Theatre Baylor Wellbeing BearStand Campus Dining Offerings Campus Recreation Credit Union Emotional Wellbeing Solutions Game Room Health Center Martin Museum of Art Massage Therapy Mayborn Museum Complex Parking Personal Technology Purchases Personal Cell Phone Discounts Real Appeal School of Music University Libraries Waco Perks Benefit Forms Benefitfocus Login Manage & Lead Getting Started Core Commitments Leadership Commitments Management Toolkits & Guides Faculty Performance Process How to Approve Timecards in Ignite Managing Performance Year-Round One on One Resources Performance Helpers Performance Improvement Plan Performance Review Process - Manager Guide Recruiting and Hiring Staff Second-Level Managers: What are they and what do they do? Staff Performance Review Process Baylor Workforce Structure Additional Resources Sabbaticals, Research Leaves, and Grants System Instructions & Access Questions Tuition & Teaching Learn & Grow Available Course Listings Chronological Available Course Listings Grow@BU Grow@BU Participant Spotlights Lead@BU Lead@BU Initiative Completions Career Tools Career Conversations Individual Development Plan Faculty Development Educational Assistance Tuition Remission Tuition Reimbursement Resources & Reporting Engage with HR Contacts askHR HRC - Human Resources Consultants Human Capital Management (HCM) Specialists Talent Advising Contact List Student Employment Faculty Senate and Staff Council Baylor Organizational Chart Employee Resource Groups - ERGs Asian American & Pacific Islander Faculty & Staff Association (AAPIFSA) Black Faculty & Staff Association (BFSA) Disability Faculty and Staff Association (DFSA) Jewish Faculty & Staff Association (JFSA) Latinx Faculty & Staff Association (LFSA) Military-Connected Faculty & Staff Association (MCFSA) Policies & Postings Fraud alert: Unemployment Claims and Identity Theft Required Annual Notices State Employment Law Postings Giving How to Report Concerns Additional Employee Resources Emotional Wellbeing Solutions (EWS) Christian Conciliation Hybrid/Remote Work Resources Office of the Provost Baylor Round Table Ignite Great Colleges to Work For® Survey Human Resources Careers & Opportunities New Faculty and Staff Steps for New Faculty Research & Learn Apply & Interview New Faculty and Staff Welcome & Orientation Steps for New Faculty New Faculty Orientation Steps for New Staff New Employee Forms Employment Forms by State Transition & Exit Contingent Workers (Auxiliaries) Other Campus Employment Visa Sponsorship and Support Additional Resources Steps for New Faculty At Baylor, you are an important part of a world class faculty and staff dedicated to teaching and research, championship athletic programs, outstanding student involvement, and a diverse community with a strong commitment to faith. As a member of our outstanding faculty, you will play a critical role in fulfilling Baylor's mission to educate men and women for worldwide leadership and service . Welcome aboard! Continue reading below to check out important steps you need to complete in preparation for your first day! First Steps for Faculty You'll receive information on how to access Ignite and complete your new hire paperwork virtually. Complete your Employment Eligibility Form (I-9) Section One prior to your first day of work. For a list of acceptable documents, please visit www.uscis.gov/i-9-central/acceptable-documents . Activate DUO to access your Baylor accounts. Activate Bear ID. Complete the Prior University Work Experience Form . Read the Benefits Overview . During the Called to BU orientation session, you will hear more about benefits and have the opportunity to ask questions. Enroll in benefits using Baylor’s Benefitfocus TM system. Review the Baylor Orientation Guide and attend a Called to BU session. Prepare to attend New Faculty Orientation hosted by the Provost's Office. Steps to Complete on Day One Access Ignite to complete your employment forms virtually. Obtain your Baylor ID card . Register your vehicle to park on campus . Steps for Success in Month One Review and enroll in your selected benefits before the end of your first 30 days via Benefitfocus TM . If you need assistance, please email askHR@baylor.edu . Review Baylor University Policies . Understand Baylor’s compensation philosophy . Check Baylor email during your first month for training sessions or requirements. Compliance Training Preventing Harassment, Discrimination, & Sexual Violence As a part of Baylor's commitment to developing a caring campus community, all faculty and staff are required annually to complete the Intersections: Preventing Harassment, Discrimination, & Sexual Violence online course in Ignite . You can read more about Baylor's Title IX policy and the role of faculty and staff members here. Occupational Safety and Health You will receive an email from the OSHA Manager with information for required training and about the RiskAnalytics/RiskTool system. The vendor for the computer-based training is RiskAnalytics/RiskTool. Once enrolled in the training system you will receive a welcome email from RiskTool to establish a password. After the welcome email, you will receive additional emails for each training module that you are assigned to complete ( These emails are not spam ). The training modules selected for each employee are part of the Occupational Safety and Health’s (OSHA) safety compliance initiative for the University. New hires are enrolled in the programs soon after the start of their employment with the university,. These modules must be completed within two weeks of the assignment date. More information is available on the Environmental Health & Safety website. University Training Database Website Succeeding in the Weeks Ahead We hope you find success in all stages of your career at Baylor. Whether you are returning to work on campus after time away, or this is your first time putting on the green and gold, we hope that Baylor feels like home. There are many resources available to help you develop professionally and personally. Tools for Professional and Personal Development Creating a Bi-Weekly Employee Timecard in Ignite Be Part of the Baylor Family Attend Baylor athletic events, visit the Mayborn Museum, exercise at the Student Life Center (SLC), enjoy a performance by Baylor Theatre students, engage with Baylor Traditions, walk the bear trail around campus, spend some time on the Brazos river and rent equipment at the Baylor marina, visit the bear habitat on campus, get some Baylor spirit gear at the bookstore, and participate in the Waco community. Baylor Human Resources Putting People First. Clifton Robinson Tower | Suite 200 700 S University Parks Dr Waco, TX 76706 One Bear Place #97053 Waco, TX 76798 askhr@baylor.edu 254-710-2000 Ask HR About Jobs Disclosures Visit Policies Human Resources Careers & Opportunities New Faculty and Staff Steps for New Faculty About Careers & Opportunities Back Research & Learn Back Staff Job Descriptions whyBaylor Apply & Interview Back Faculty Application Process Staff Application Process Veteran Resources for Interviewing New Faculty and Staff Back Welcome & Orientation Back Living in Waco Steps for New Faculty Back New Faculty Orientation Steps for New Staff New Employee Forms Back Completing Your I-9 Back FAQs for Completing Your I-9 Employment Forms by State Transition & Exit Back Exiting Faculty Exiting Staff Contingent Workers (Auxiliaries) Other Campus Employment Back Summer Camp Employment Visa Sponsorship and Support Back Hiring and Support of International Scholars Next Steps for International Scholars Additional Resources Benefits & Advantages Back My Benefits Back Veteran Resources Baylor Wellbeing Enrollment Back Benefitfocus Information Benefitfocus Login 2026 Benefits Guide What's New for 2026 Retirement Back Investing in Your Retirement Back Baylor 457(b) Plan Baylor Retirement Plan - 403(b) Importance of Retirement Planning TIAA Updates - New Features Preparing for Your Retirement Back Retiree Insurance Detai