Campus Recreation Credit Union Emotional Wellbeing Solutions Game Room Health Center Martin Museum of Art Massage Therapy Mayborn Museum Complex Parking Personal Technology Purchases Personal Cell Phone Discounts Real Appeal School of Music University Libraries Waco Perks Benefit Forms Benefitfocus Login Manage & Lead Getting Started Core Commitments Leadership Commitments Management Toolkits & Guides Faculty Performance Process How to Approve Timecards in Ignite Managing Performance Year-Round One on One Resources Performance Helpers Performance Improvement Plan Performance Review Process - Manager Guide Recruiting and Hiring Staff Second-Level Managers: What are they and what do they do? Staff Performance Review Process Baylor Workforce Structure Additional Resources Sabbaticals, Research Leaves, and Grants System Instructions & Access Questions Tuition & Teaching Learn & Grow Available Course Listings Chronological Available Course Listings Grow@BU Grow@BU Participant Spotlights Lead@BU Lead@BU Initiative Completions Career Tools Career Conversations Individual Development Plan Faculty Development Educational Assistance Tuition Remission Tuition Reimbursement Resources & Reporting Engage with HR Contacts askHR HRC - Human Resources Consultants Human Capital Management (HCM) Specialists Talent Advising Contact List Student Employment Faculty Senate and Staff Council Baylor Organizational Chart Employee Resource Groups - ERGs Asian American & Pacific Islander Faculty & Staff Association (AAPIFSA) Black Faculty & Staff Association (BFSA) Disability Faculty and Staff Association (DFSA) Jewish Faculty & Staff Association (JFSA) Latinx Faculty & Staff Association (LFSA) Military-Connected Faculty & Staff Association (MCFSA) Policies & Postings Fraud alert: Unemployment Claims and Identity Theft Required Annual Notices State Employment Law Postings Giving How to Report Concerns Additional Employee Resources Emotional Wellbeing Solutions (EWS) Christian Conciliation Hybrid/Remote Work Resources Office of the Provost Baylor Round Table Ignite Great Colleges to Work For® Survey Human Resources Careers & Opportunities New Faculty and Staff Steps for New Staff Research & Learn Apply & Interview New Faculty and Staff Welcome & Orientation Steps for New Faculty Steps for New Staff New Employee Forms Employment Forms by State Transition & Exit Contingent Workers (Auxiliaries) Other Campus Employment Visa Sponsorship and Support Additional Resources Steps for New Staff At Baylor, you will find a world class faculty and staff dedicated to teaching and research, championship athletic programs, outstanding student involvement and a diverse community with a strong commitment to faith. As a staff member, you will find a supportive work environment dedicated to excellence and service. The people of the university make Baylor special, and you now have the opportunity to contribute to and receive the benefit of that effort. Your employment at Baylor begins with Called to BU. Follow the steps below to prepare for your first day: Steps to Prepare for Called to BU (Orientation) You'll receive information on how to access Ignite and complete your new hire paperwork virtually. Complete your Employment Eligibility Form (I-9) Section One prior to your first day of work. For a list of acceptable documents, please visit www.uscis.gov/i-9-central/acceptable-documents . Activate DUO to access your Baylor accounts. Activate BearID . Complete the Prior University Work Experience Form . Read the Benefits Enrollment Resources . During orientation, you will hear more about benefits and have the opportunity to ask questions to a benefits specialist. Review the Welcome to Baylor page on the HR website. Review the Baylor Orientation Guide . Review the Payroll page and prepare any questions for your manager. Steps to Complete on Day One Access Ignite to complete your employment forms virtually. View this webpage for instructions to digitally register your vehicle and to obtain your digital Baylor ID. Steps for Success in Month One Review and enroll in your selected benefits before the end of your first 30 days via Benefitfocus TM . Review Baylor University Policies . Understand Baylor’s compensation philosophy . Check Baylor email during your first month for training sessions or requirements. Compliance Training Preventing Harassment, Discrimination, & Sexual Violence and Your Role as Baylor Staff As a part of Baylor's commitment to developing a caring campus community, all faculty and staff are required annually to complete the Intersections: Preventing Harassment, Discrimination, & Sexual Violence online course in Ignite . You can read more about Baylor's Title IX policy and the role of faculty and staff members here. As well, learn more about your role in reporting according to Senate Bill 212 . Occupational Safety and Health You will receive an email from the OSHA Manager with information for required training and about the RiskAnalytics/RiskTool system. The vendor for the computer-based training is RiskAnalytics/RiskTool. Once enrolled in the training system you will receive a welcome email from RiskTool to establish a password. After the welcome email, you will receive additional emails for each training module that you are assigned to complete ( These emails are not spam ). The training modules selected for each employee are part of the Occupational Safety and Health’s (OSHA) safety compliance initiative for the University. New hires are enrolled in the programs soon after the start of their employment with the university,. These modules must be completed within two weeks of the assignment date. More information is available on the Environmental Health & Safety website. University Training Database Website Succeeding in the Weeks Ahead We hope you find success in all stages of your career at Baylor. Whether you are returning to work on campus after time away, or this is your first time putting on the green and gold, we hope that Baylor feels like home. There are many resources available to help you develop professionally and personally. Tools for Professional and Personal Development HR Contacts & Resources View the Waco Culture Guide Be Part of the Baylor Family Attend Baylor athletic events, visit the Mayborn Museum, exercise at the Student Life Center (SLC), enjoy a performance by Baylor Theatre students, engage with Baylor Traditions, walk the bear trail around campus, spend some time on the Brazos river and rent equipment at the Baylor marina, visit the bear habitat on campus, get some Baylor spirit gear at the bookstore, and participate in the Waco community. Baylor Human Resources Putting People First. Clifton Robinson Tower | Suite 200 700 S University Parks Dr Waco, TX 76706 One Bear Place #97053 Waco, TX 76798 askhr@baylor.edu 254-710-2000 Ask HR About Jobs Disclosures Visit Policies Human Resources Careers & Opportunities New Faculty and Staff Steps for New Staff About Careers & Opportunities Back Research & Learn Back Staff Job Descriptions whyBaylor Apply & Interview Back Faculty Application Process Staff Application Process Veteran Resources for Interviewing New Faculty and Staff Back Welcome & Orientation Back Living in Waco Steps for New Faculty Back New Faculty Orientation Steps for New Staff New Employee Forms Back Completing Your I-9 Back FAQs for Completing Your I-9 Employment Forms by State Transition & Exit Back Exiting Faculty Exiting Staff Contingent Workers (Auxiliaries) Other Campus Employment Back Summer Camp Employment Visa Sponsorship and Support Back Hiring and Support of International Scholars Next Steps for International Scholars Additional Resources Benefits & Advantages Back My Benefits Back Veteran Resources Baylor Wellbeing Enrollment Back Benefitfocus Information Benefitfocus Login 2026 Benefits Guide What's New for 2026 Retirement Back Investing in Your Retirement Back Baylor 457(b) Plan Baylor Retirement Plan - 403(b) Importance of Retirement 