us Recreation Credit Union Emotional Wellbeing Solutions Game Room Health Center Martin Museum of Art Massage Therapy Mayborn Museum Complex Parking Personal Technology Purchases Personal Cell Phone Discounts Real Appeal School of Music University Libraries Waco Perks Benefit Forms Benefitfocus Login Manage & Lead Getting Started Core Commitments Leadership Commitments Management Toolkits & Guides Faculty Performance Process How to Approve Timecards in Ignite Managing Performance Year-Round One on One Resources Performance Helpers Performance Improvement Plan Performance Review Process - Manager Guide Recruiting and Hiring Staff Second-Level Managers: What are they and what do they do? Staff Performance Review Process Baylor Workforce Structure Additional Resources Sabbaticals, Research Leaves, and Grants System Instructions & Access Questions Tuition & Teaching Learn & Grow Available Course Listings Chronological Available Course Listings Grow@BU Grow@BU Participant Spotlights Lead@BU Lead@BU Initiative Completions Career Tools Career Conversations Individual Development Plan Faculty Development Educational Assistance Tuition Remission Tuition Reimbursement Resources & Reporting Engage with HR Contacts askHR HRC - Human Resources Consultants Human Capital Management (HCM) Specialists Talent Advising Contact List Student Employment Faculty Senate and Staff Council Baylor Organizational Chart Employee Resource Groups - ERGs Asian American & Pacific Islander Faculty & Staff Association (AAPIFSA) Black Faculty & Staff Association (BFSA) Disability Faculty and Staff Association (DFSA) Jewish Faculty & Staff Association (JFSA) Latinx Faculty & Staff Association (LFSA) Military-Connected Faculty & Staff Association (MCFSA) Policies & Postings Fraud alert: Unemployment Claims and Identity Theft Required Annual Notices State Employment Law Postings Giving How to Report Concerns Additional Employee Resources Emotional Wellbeing Solutions (EWS) Christian Conciliation Hybrid/Remote Work Resources Office of the Provost Baylor Round Table Ignite Great Colleges to Work For® Survey Human Resources Careers & Opportunities Transition & Exit Exiting Faculty Research & Learn Apply & Interview New Faculty and Staff Transition & Exit Exiting Faculty Exiting Staff Contingent Workers (Auxiliaries) Other Campus Employment Visa Sponsorship and Support Additional Resources Exiting Faculty In This Guide Information for Exiting Faculty Steps to Complete Prior to Your Last Day Information About Exiting Faculty Email Accounts Resources Information for Exiting Faculty Steps to Complete Prior to Your Last Day Read the Faculty Dismissal Policy and/or the Retirement Benefits policies. Submit a letter of resignation to your supervisor and/or department head. The letter should include the following information: Reason for resignation Position title Expected date of separation (a two-week notice required) Signature of separating employee. Complete the Exiting the University Journey assigned to you in Ignite . Review all tasks assigned to you prior to your last day and complete all that apply including the Technology Access Form. Update your personal record in Ignite with your forwarding address for end-of-the-year W-2 mail outs. Complete the Faculty Exit Survey Complete and upload the Technology Access Form to your Ignite Exit Journey. Additional actions required by the separating employee prior to last day of employment: Return library books to the appropriate University Libraries; Pay or arrange to pay any indebtedness owed to the University or related entity; Remove any personal or private files from your computer; and Coordinate separation with Student Financial Aid Office if you, your spouse and/or your dependents are receiving tuition remission benefits. If you are a faculty member who was lead within a lab, please complete the Lab Decommissioning Form before your last day. Information About Exiting Faculty Email Accounts Faculty voluntarily separating from the University will retain your faculty email for approximately six (6) months after your last day of employment. These accounts are deleted after the six month time period(without prior notification)unless the individual re-affiliates with Baylor through employment or school enrollment. Individuals involuntarily separated from the University will lose access immediately. Email accounts for retirees currently remain active for an indefinite period. Baylor currently provides former students an email account (BearID@alumni.baylor.edu) that allows them to continue to show their Baylor affiliation through their email address. If you meet the established level for provisioning of alumni accounts (see below), contact the helpdesk at 710-4357 or email helpdesk@baylor.edu to learn more on how to accessing this account. For more information on Alumni Email, please visit t he ITS Alumni Email page . Resources for Exiting Faculty Technology Access Change Form Baylor Human Resources Putting People First. Clifton Robinson Tower | Suite 200 700 S University Parks Dr Waco, TX 76706 One Bear Place #97053 Waco, TX 76798 askhr@baylor.edu 254-710-2000 Ask HR About Jobs Disclosures Visit Policies Human Resources Careers & Opportunities Transition & Exit Exiting Faculty About Careers & Opportunities Back Research & Learn Back Staff Job Descriptions whyBaylor Apply & Interview Back Faculty Application Process Staff Application Process Veteran Resources for Interviewing New Faculty and Staff Back Welcome & Orientation Back Living in Waco Steps for New Faculty Back New Faculty Orientation Steps for New Staff New Employee Forms Back Completing Your I-9 Back FAQs for Completing Your I-9 Employment Forms by State Transition & Exit Back Exiting Faculty Exiting Staff Contingent Workers (Auxiliaries) Other Campus Employment Back Summer Camp Employment Visa Sponsorship and Support Back Hiring and Support of International Scholars Next Steps for International Scholars Additional Resources Benefit