      "title": "Exiting Staff",
      "description": "Exiting Staff | Human Resources | Baylor University Skip to main content Skip to main navigation Open Mobile Navigation Human Resources About Careers & Opportunities Research & Learn Staff Job Descriptions whyBaylor Apply & Interview Faculty Application Process Staff Application Process Veteran Resources for Interviewing New Faculty and Staff Welcome & Orientation Steps for New Faculty Steps for New Staff New Employee Forms Employment Forms by State Transition & Exit Exiting Faculty Exiting Staff Contingent Workers (Auxiliaries) Other Campus Employment Summer Camp Employment Visa Sponsorship and Support Hiring and Support of International Scholars Next Steps for International Scholars Additional Resources Benefits & Advantages My Benefits Veteran Resources Baylor Wellbeing Enrollment Benefitfocus Information Benefitfocus Login 2026 Benefits Guide What's New for 2026 Retirement Investing in Your Retirement Preparing for Your Retirement Enjoying Your Retirement Retiree Advantages Retiree Benefits Overview Compensation Compensation Philosophy and Resources Total Compensation Statement Fair Labor Standards Act (FLSA) Merit Insurance Offerings Medical Insurance Plans Prescription Drug Plan Dental Insurance Plan Vision Insurance Plan Employer Provided Insurances Retiree Insurance Details Continuation of Insurance Coverage Voluntary Supplemental Insurances Pet Insurance Employee Recognition Tuition Remission Time Off & Leave Policies Family and Medical Leave Act (FMLA) Maternity and Primary Caregiver Leave Paid Caregiver Leave Paid Parental Leave Timecards During University Closures Employee Caregiver & Family Resources Adoption Assistance Program Crisis Resources Care.com Spousal Employment Assistance Educational Assistance Expectant & New Parents Progyny Surviving Spouse Benefits Baylor Advantages Athletic Tickets Baby Bear Program Baylor Bookstore Baylor Club at McLane Stadium Baylor Theatre Baylor Wellbeing BearStand Campus Dining Offerings Campus Recreation Credit Union Emotional Wellbeing Solutions Game Room Health Center Martin Museum of Art Massage Therapy Mayborn Museum Complex Parking Personal Technology Purchases Personal Cell Phone Discounts Real Appeal School of Music University Libraries Waco Perks Benefit Forms Benefitfocus Login Manage & Lead Getting Started Core Commitments Leadership Commitments Management Toolkits & Guides Faculty Performance Process How to Approve Timecards in Ignite Managing Performance Year-Round One on One Resources Performance Helpers Performance Improvement Plan Performance Review Process - Manager Guide Recruiting and Hiring Staff Second-Level Managers: What are they and what do they do? Staff Performance Review Process Baylor Workforce Structure Additional Resources Sabbaticals, Research Leaves, and Grants System Instructions & Access Questions Tuition & Teaching Learn & Grow Available Course Listings Chronological Available Course Listings Grow@BU Grow@BU Participant Spotlights Lead@BU Lead@BU Initiative Completions Career Tools Career Conversations Individual Development Plan Faculty Development Educational Assistance Tuition Remission Tuition Reimbursement Resources & Reporting Engage with HR Contacts askHR HRC - Human Resources Consultants Human Capital Management (HCM) Specialists Talent Advising Contact List Student Employment Faculty Senate and Staff Council Baylor Organizational Chart Employee Resource Groups - ERGs Asian American & Pacific Islander Faculty & Staff Association (AAPIFSA) Black Faculty & Staff Association (BFSA) Disability Faculty and Staff Association (DFSA) Jewish Faculty & Staff Association (JFSA) Latinx Faculty & Staff Association (LFSA) Military-Connected Faculty & Staff Association (MCFSA) Policies & Postings Fraud alert: Unemployment Claims and Identity Theft Required Annual Notices State Employment Law Postings Giving How to Report Concerns Additional Employee Resources Emotional Wellbeing Solutions (EWS) Christian Conciliation Hybrid/Remote Work Resources Office of the Provost Baylor Round Table Ignite Great Colleges to Work For® Survey Human Resources Careers & Opportunities Transition & Exit Exiting Staff Research & Learn Apply & Interview New Faculty and Staff Transition & Exit Exiting Faculty Exiting Staff Contingent Workers (Auxiliaries) Other Campus Employment Visa Sponsorship and Support Additional Resources Exiting Staff In This Guide Information for Exiting Staff Steps to Complete Prior to Your Last Day Information About Exiting Staff Email Accounts Resources Information for Exiting Staff Staff who are voluntarily separating from the university must provide at least two (2) weeks’ notice to their supervisor. Accrued vacation and/or holidays do not extend employment. In other words, an employee may not complete a final period of employment through the use of accrued vacation or holiday entitlement. The date of termination should be for the final day worked in the department. Accrued but unused vacation time has cash value and upon separation from the University, Baylor will pay for accrued vacation balances up to the maximum payout levels in the table shown below. Service Years Maximum Payout at Separation 0-4 80 hours 5-9 100 hours 10-14 120 hours 15-19 160 hours 20+ 200 hours Example 1: An employee who has 4 years of service with 40 hours of accrued and unused vacation time at separation will be paid for 40 hours of unused vacation time in his / her final paycheck. Example 2: An employee who has 8 years of service with 200 hours of accrued and unused vacation time at separation will be paid for 100 hours of unused vacation time in his / her final paycheck. Balances used to determine maximum payout at separation will be determined as follows: If an employee’s separation date is any day other than the last day of the employees pay period, the maximum payout balance will be determined by using the employees vacation time balance as of the end of the previous pay period less any vacation time taken in the current pay period. If the employee’s separation date is on the last day of the pay period, the maximum payout balance will be their vacation time balance as of their separation date. See these policies for helpful information about the exiting staff process: Staff Vacation Policy Staff Separation Policy Retirement Benefits Policy Steps to Complete Prior to Your Last Day Submit a letter of resignation to your supervisor and/or department head. The letter should include the following information: Reason for resignation; Position title; Expected date of separation, a two-week notice required; and Signature of separating employee. Complete the Exiting the University Journey assigned to you in Ignite . Review all tasks assigned to you prior to your last day and complete all that apply including the Technology Access Form. Update your personal record in Ignite with your forwarding address for end-of-the-year W-2 mail outs. Complete the Staff Exit Survey Complete and upload the Technology Access Form to your Ignite Exit Journey. Additional actions required by the separating employee prior to last day of employment: Return library books to the appropriate University Libraries; Pay or arrange to pay any indebtedness owed to the University or related entity; Remove any personal or private files from your computer; and Coordinate separation with Student Financial Aid Office if you, your spouse and/or your dependents are receiving tuition remission benefits. Information About Exiting Staff Email Accounts Staff voluntarily leaving the University will have their email account deactivated at 11:59 PM on your last day of employment. Individuals involuntarily separated from the University will lose access immediately. Email accounts for retirees currently remain active for an indefinite period. Baylor currently provides former students an email account (BearID@alumni.baylor.edu) that allows them to continue to show their Baylor affiliation through their email address. If you meet the established level for provisioning of alumni accounts (see below), contact the Helpdesk at 710-4357 or email, helpdesk@baylor.edu , to learn more on how to accessing this account. For more information on Alumni Email, please visit the ITS Alumni Email Page . Resources-Exiting Staff Technology Access Change Form Baylor Human Resources Putting People First. Clifton Robinson Tower | Suite 200 700 S University Parks Dr Waco, TX 76706 One Bear Place #97053 Waco, TX 76798 askhr@baylor.edu 254-710-2000 Ask HR About Jobs Disclosures Visit Policies Human Resources Careers & Opportunities Transition & Exit Exiting Staff About Careers & Opportunities Back Research & Learn Back Staff Job Descriptions whyBaylor Apply & Interview Back Faculty Application Process Staff Application Process Veteran Resources for Interviewing New Faculty and Staff Back Welcome & Orientation Back Living in Waco Steps for New Faculty Back New Faculty Orientation Steps for New Staff New Employee Forms Back Completing Your I-9 Back FAQs for Completing Your I-9 Employment Forms by State Transition & Exit Back Exiting Faculty Exiting Staff Contingent Workers (Auxiliaries) Other Campus Employment Back Summer Camp Employment Visa Sponsorship and Support Back Hiring and Support of International Scholars Next Steps for International Scholars Additional Resources Benefits & Advantages Back My Benefits Back Veteran Resources Baylor Wellbeing Enrollment Back Benefitfocus Information Benefitfocus Login 2026 Benefits Guide What's New for 2026 Retirement Back Investing in Your Retirement Back Baylor 457(b) Plan Baylor Retirement Plan - 403(b) Importance of Retirement Planning TIAA Updates - New Features Preparing for Your Retirement Back Retiree Insurance Details Back Health Reimbursement Account (HRA) Medicare Basic Information Retiring Process Checklist Enjoying Your Retirement Back My Retiree Benefits Technology Benefits for Retirees Retiree Tuition Remission Retiree Important Contact List Retire