tion Hybrid/Remote Work Resources Office of the Provost Baylor Round Table Ignite Great Colleges to Work For® Survey Human Resources Careers & Opportunities Visa Sponsorship and Support Research & Learn Apply & Interview New Faculty and Staff Transition & Exit Contingent Workers (Auxiliaries) Other Campus Employment Visa Sponsorship and Support Hiring and Support of International Scholars Next Steps for International Scholars Additional Resources Visa Sponsorship and Support What is Visa Sponsorship and Support? Visa Sponsorship and Support at Baylor University aims to provide clear, consistent, and helpful resources for international scholars to gain employment within our various University departments and research initiatives. International Scholar Visa Support and Sponsorship Baylor Human Resources International Employment provides services and support to all international scholars employed by the university and the departments that they are a part of. We coordinate with teams across the campus to offer sponsorship through various programs H1 and J1 visas. Our goal is to welcome you on campus and be an ongoing resource throughout your time with Baylor. International Scholars are individuals who currently do not have citizenship or permanent residence through the United States of America and require sponsored or unsponsored work authorization to be employed at Baylor University. Visa Process Use the links below for more information on J-I and H-Ib Visas. J-I Visa Working in the United States: Exchange Visitors H-Ib Working in the United States: H-Ib Specialty Occupations Departmental Visa Support If you are a current Baylor University faculty or staff member involved in the hiring or management of International Scholars, please use the link below to access important information and resources. Hiring and Support of International Scholars Current International Scholars Are you a current international scholar? The Baylor Human Resources department provides direct guidance and support during your time with us. We partner with your manager, HRC, and others across campus to help you with questions, concerns, or needs that you may come across during this time. Questions can be emailed directly to askHR@baylor.edu and we will be excited to help you. Resources Once hired by Baylor University, International Scholars should use the following link to access resources related to job acceptance, onboarding, relocation, and more. Next Steps for International Scholars Questions? If you have specific questions regarding Visa Sponsorship and Support that are not answered on this website, please email International_Employment@baylor.edu . Baylor Human Resources Putting People First. Clifton Robinson Tower | Suite 200 700 S University Parks Dr Waco, TX 76706 One Bear Place #97053 Waco, TX 76798 askhr@baylor.edu 254-710-2000 Ask HR About Jobs Disclosures Visit Policies Human Resources Careers & Opportunities Visa Sponsorship and Support About Careers & Opportunities Back Research & Learn Back Staff Job Descriptions whyBaylor Apply & Interview Back Faculty Application Process Staff Application Process Veteran Resources for Interviewing New Faculty and Staff Back Welcome & Orientation Back Living in Waco Steps for New Faculty Back New Faculty Orientation Steps for New Staff New Employee Forms Back Completing Your I-9 Back FAQs for Completing Your I-9 Employment Forms by State Transition & Exit Back Exiting Faculty Exiting Staff Contingent Workers (Auxiliaries) Other Campus Employment Back Summer Camp Employment Visa Sponsorship and Support Back Hiring and Support of International Scholars Next Steps for International Scholars Additional Resources Benefits & Advantages Back My Benefits Back Veteran Resources Baylor Wellbeing Enrollment Back Benefitfocus Information Benefitfocus Login 2026 Benefits Guide What's New for 2026 Retirement Back Investing in Your Retirement Back Baylor 457(b) Plan Baylor Retirement Plan - 403(b) Importance of Retirement P