 Conciliation Hybrid/Remote Work Resources Office of the Provost Baylor Round Table Ignite Great Colleges to Work For® Survey Human Resources Careers & Opportunities Visa Sponsorship and Support Next Steps for International Scholars Research & Learn Apply & Interview New Faculty and Staff Transition & Exit Contingent Workers (Auxiliaries) Other Campus Employment Visa Sponsorship and Support Hiring and Support of International Scholars Next Steps for International Scholars Additional Resources Next Steps for International Scholars Baylor sponsors International Scholars at the Faculty and Postdoctoral staff throughout the university on a departmental basis. If you have questions about sponsorship for any role, feel free to ask your main point of contact or recruiter during the hiring process. You are not required to divulge the need for sponsorship prior to the offer being extended and accepted. Not all positions are granted sponsorship. Carefully read each job posting paying special attention to the language regarding eligibility to work in the US. Resources for Applicants & New Hires Application Process - Click below to find out more about the hiring process for both Faculty and Staff. Postdoctoral roles at Baylor are considered staff. Faculty Application Process Postdoctoral (Staff) Application Process Accepting the Job Offer Once you have accepted an offer with the University, inform your recruiter or contact that you will need sponsorship for employment. A Baylor HR International Talent Advisor will work with you to evaluate your specific sponsorship needs and help you understand what is available with the position you have accepted. Once you have decided on the appropriate U.S. visa you wish to pursue, the IE Talent Advisor will continue to walk you through the process. A background check will be performed through a third-party company. After your background check has successfully completed and your Visa has been approved, your IE Talent Advisor will begin helping you with any Baylor provided relocation assistance. Be sure to keep your IE Talent Advisor informed of any changes in your travel, visa status, or personal circumstances that would change the date of arrival. Complete onboarding tasks in Ignite. Relocation Information - Moving to Waco Texas & Baylor University Baylor University is committed to providing a comprehensive international employment process.  Below you will find several resources to assist your transition to Baylor University once hired.  If you have any questions during this process, please email International_Employment@baylor.edu . Waco is a city at the heart of the state of Texas. A large sprawling state with a diverse population and many different natural resources and features. Your move to Waco will be an exiting time, and your HR International Employment Talent Advisors are here to help. A multitude of options for education of your young ones, housing, and leisure activities are available. Below you will find some resources to start you in your journey. Learn more about Baylor and our strategic vision, Baylor In Deeds . Explore our great hometown of Waco and the many opportunities to engage locally. If you are new to Central Texas, This is Waco! Waco Area Secondary and Elementary Schools Information about Waco, Texas Social Security Administration Waco Cultural Guide Discover Waco Baylor Human Resources Putting People First. Clifton Robinson Tower | Suite 200 700 S University Parks Dr Waco, TX 76706 One Bear Place #97053 Waco, TX 76798 askhr@baylor.edu 254-710-2000 Ask HR About Jobs Disclosures Visit Policies Human Resources Careers & Opportunities Visa Sponsorship and Support Next Steps for International Scholars About Careers & Opportunities Back Research & Learn Back Staff Job Descriptions whyBaylor Apply & Interview Back Faculty Application Process Staff Application Process Veteran Resources for Interviewing New Faculty and Staff Back Welcome & Orientation Back Living in Waco Steps for New 