      "description": "Fraud alert: Unemployment Claims and Identity Theft | Human Resources | Baylor University Skip to main content Skip to main navigation Open Mobile Navigation Human Resources About Careers & Opportunities Research & Learn Staff Job Descriptions whyBaylor Apply & Interview Faculty Application Process Staff Application Process Veteran Resources for Interviewing New Faculty and Staff Welcome & Orientation Steps for New Faculty Steps for New Staff New Employee Forms Employment Forms by State Transition & Exit Exiting Faculty Exiting Staff Contingent Workers (Auxiliaries) Other Campus Employment Summer Camp Employment Visa Sponsorship and Support Hiring and Support of International Scholars Next Steps for International Scholars Additional Resources Benefits & Advantages My Benefits Veteran Resources Baylor Wellbeing Enrollment Benefitfocus Information Benefitfocus Login 2026 Benefits Guide What's New for 2026 Retirement Investing in Your Retirement Preparing for Your Retirement Enjoying Your Retirement Retiree Advantages Retiree Benefits Overview Compensation Compensation Philosophy and Resources Total Compensation Statement Fair Labor Standards Act (FLSA) Merit Insurance Offerings Medical Insurance Plans Prescription Drug Plan Dental Insurance Plan Vision Insurance Plan Employer Provided Insurances Retiree Insurance Details Continuation of Insurance Coverage Voluntary Supplemental Insurances Pet Insurance Employee Recognition Tuition Remission Time Off & Leave Policies Family and Medical Leave Act (FMLA) Maternity and Primary Caregiver Leave Paid Caregiver Leave Paid Parental Leave Timecards During University Closures Employee Caregiver & Family Resources Adoption Assistance Program Crisis Resources Care.com Spousal Employment Assistance Educational Assistance Expectant & New Parents Progyny Surviving Spouse Benefits Baylor Advantages Athletic Tickets Baby Bear Program Baylor Bookstore Baylor Club at McLane Stadium Baylor Theatre Baylor Wellbeing BearStand Campus Dining Offerings Campus Recreation Credit Union Emotional Wellbeing Solutions Game Room Health Center Martin Museum of Art Massage Therapy Mayborn Museum Complex Parking Personal Technology Purchases Personal Cell Phone Discounts Real Appeal School of Music University Libraries Waco Perks Benefit Forms Benefitfocus Login Manage & Lead Getting Started Core Commitments Leadership Commitments Management Toolkits & Guides Faculty Performance Process How to Approve Timecards in Ignite Managing Performance Year-Round One on One Resources Performance Helpers Performance Improvement Plan Performance Review Process - Manager Guide Recruiting and Hiring Staff Second-Level Managers: What are they and what do they do? Staff Performance Review Process Baylor Workforce Structure Additional Resources Sabbaticals, Research Leaves, and Grants System Instructions & Access Questions Tuition & Teaching Learn & Grow Available Course Listings Chronological Available Course Listings Grow@BU Grow@BU Participant Spotlights Lead@BU Lead@BU Initiative Completions Career Tools Career Conversations Individual Development Plan Faculty Development Educational Assistance Tuition Remission Tuition Reimbursement Resources & Reporting Engage with HR Contacts askHR HRC - Human Resources Consultants Human Capital Management (HCM) Specialists Talent Advising Contact List Student Employment Faculty Senate and Staff Council Baylor Organizational Chart Employee Resource Groups - ERGs Asian American & Pacific Islander Faculty & Staff Association (AAPIFSA) Black Faculty & Staff Association (BFSA) Disability Faculty and Staff Association (DFSA) Jewish Faculty & Staff Association (JFSA) Latinx Faculty & Staff Association (LFSA) Military-Connected Faculty & Staff Association (MCFSA) Policies & Postings Fraud alert: Unemployment Claims and Identity Theft Required Annual Notices State Employment Law Postings Giving How to Report Concerns Additional Employee Resources Emotional Wellbeing Solutions (EWS) Christian Conciliation Hybrid/Remote Work Resources Office of the Provost Baylor Round Table Ignite Great Colleges to Work For® Survey Human Resources Resources & Reporting Policies & Postings Fraud alert: Unemployment Claims and Identity Theft Engage with HR Contacts Employee Resource Groups - ERGs Policies & Postings Fraud alert: Unemployment Claims and Identity Theft Required Annual Notices State Employment Law Postings Giving How to Report Concerns Additional Employee Resources Fraud alert: Unemployment Claims and Identity Theft Across the United States, state unemployment offices have been receiving an ever-increasing number of fraudulent claims from people claiming to be someone else. Colleges and universities are no exception, and Baylor has been receiving such claims from people fraudulently assuming the identity of our faculty or staff. As such, all Baylor faculty and staff are urged to take precautions against identity theft and notify Baylor Human Resources if they receive mail from Texas Workforce Commission (TWC) or other state agency about unemployment claims and take other steps as identified below. With the start of the new year, it is a good time to take the opportunity to refresh your personal passwords and take other measures to keep yourself secure from identity theft by taking actions recommended by the Texas Attorney General . To be clear, there has been no evidence of a breach in any TWC system nor in Baylor University’s systems. This fraud is occurring across the nation regardless of any breach in computer systems. According to TWC, Texas has seen an unprecedented increase in the number of unemployment claims. Potential fraud was connected to more than 4,500 unemployment claims in Texas this year. In many of these fraudulent cases, unsuspecting Texans were the targets of identity theft, then had their stolen identities used to make unemployment claims. In most cases, bad actors appear to have obtained password or private information from the individuals in question through direct hacking or phishing as stated in the TWC news media. For those who find themselves a victim of a fraudulent unemployment claim, we suggest the following steps: If a current employee, contact the Baylor Human Resources department so we can file a fraud claim. If you receive a letter from TWC asking for repayment based on a fraudulent claim, you should follow the instructions included in the letter on how to appeal the decision or contact Human Resources for assistance. Report any fraudulent claim with TWC Unemployment Insurance division fraud submission portal found on the TWC homepage . To report unemployment benefits related issues, please contact the Texas Workforce Commission at 1-800-252-3642. Complaints may also be submitted via email to twc.fraud@twc.state.tx.us . Utilize the Employee Assistance Resources available here to include LegalConnect and FinancialConnect for resources and support due to Identity Theft. File a fraud report with the local police or sheriff department, drivers’ license office, and other agencies. More information on reporting Identity Theft is available from the Texas Department of Public Safety . Contact major credit bureaus such as Experian , TransUnion , and Equifax , since the breach may involve social security numbers, birth dates, and other personal information. Contact your banking institution and any creditors to make them aware of the situation. Review the U.S. Department of Justice Unemployment Insurance Fraud Consumer Protection Guide . Baylor Human Resources wants to partner with our employees to protect their personal information and support the reporting of fraudulent claims. Contact us at askHR@baylor.edu or 254-710-2000 for any questions. Baylor Human Resources Putting People First. Clifton Robinson Tower | Suite 200 700 S University Parks Dr Waco, TX 76706 One Bear Place #97053 Waco, TX 76798 askhr@baylor.edu 254-710-2000 Ask HR About Jobs Disclosures Visit Policies Human Resources Resources & Reporting Policies & Postings Fraud alert: Unemployment Claims and Identity Theft About Careers & Opportunities Back Research & Learn Back Staff Job Descriptions whyBaylor Apply & Interview Back Faculty Application Process Staff Application Process Veteran Resources for Interviewing New Faculty and Staff Back Welcome & Orientation Back Living in Waco Steps for New Faculty Back New Faculty Orientation Steps for New Staff New Employee Forms Back Completing Your I-9 Back FAQs for Completing Your I-9 Employment Forms by State Transition & Exit Back Exiting Faculty Exiting Staff Contingent Workers (Auxiliaries) Other Campus Employment Back Summer Camp Employment Visa Sponsorship and Support Back Hiring and Support of International Scholars Next Steps for International Scholars Additional Resources Benefits & Advantages Back My Benefits Back Veteran Resources Baylor Wellbeing Enrollment Back Benefitfocus Information Benefitfocus Login 2026 Benefits Guide What's New for 2026 Retirement Back Investing in Your Retirement Back Baylor 457(b) Plan Baylor Retirement Plan - 403(b) Importance of Retirement Planning TIAA Updates - New Features Preparing for Your Retirement Back Retiree Insurance Details Back Health Reimbursement Account (HRA) Medicare Basic Information Retiring Process Checklist Enjoying Your Retirement Back My Retiree Benefits Technology Benefits for Retirees Retiree Tuition Remission Retiree Important Contact List Retiree Advantages Retiree Benefits Overview Compensation Back Compensation Philosophy and Resources Total Compensation Statement Fair Labor Standards Act (FLSA) Merit Insurance Offerings Back Medical Insurance Plans Back Flexible Spending Accounts (FSA) Health Savings Account (HSA) Livongo Prescription Drug Plan Dental Insurance Plan Vision Insurance Plan Employer Provided Insurances Retiree Insurance Details Continuation of Insurance Coverage Voluntary Supplemental Insurances Pet Insurance Employee Recognition Tuition Remission Time 