Hybrid/Remote Work Resources Office of the Provost Baylor Round Table Ignite Great Colleges to Work For® Survey Human Resources Resources & Reporting Policies & Postings Required Annual Notices Engage with HR Contacts Employee Resource Groups - ERGs Policies & Postings Fraud alert: Unemployment Claims and Identity Theft Required Annual Notices State Employment Law Postings Giving How to Report Concerns Additional Employee Resources Required Annual Notices 2025 Annual Notice of Right to Participate in 403(b) Plan In compliance with the 403(b) regulations, this is notification of the availability of a 403(b) plan in which voluntary pre-tax and Roth elective deferrals can be made. Baylor Retirement Plan Summary of Plan Provisions Annual Medicare Part D Certification of Creditable Coverage This is a notice to all active employees and covered dependents eligible for Medicare and enrolled in Baylor University's Medical PPO/Prescription plan. www.cms.gov Annual Women's Health/Cancer Rights The Women's Health and Cancer Rights Act of 1998. Women's Health & Cancer Rights DOL.gov UMR/United Healthcare (2026) Under the health care reform law, the Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act of 2010 (PPACA), all issuers of health insurance are required to provide individuals with standard information about their health plan - a summary of benefits and coverage (SBC). Summary of Benefits and Coverage for PPO Summary of Benefits and Coverage for HDHP UMR/United Healthcare (2025) Under the health care reform law, the Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act of 2010 (PPACA), all issuers of health insurance are required to provide individuals with standard information about their health plan - a summary of benefits and coverage (SBC). Summary of Benefits and Coverage for PPO Summary of Benefits and Coverage for HDHP CHIP Notice If you or your children are eligible for Medicaid or CHIP and you are eligible for health coverage from your employer, your State may have a premium assistance program that can help pay for coverage. CHIPRA Notice Effective April 1, 2009, the Children's Health Insurance Program Reauthorization Act of 2009 (\"CHIPRA\") adds two new special enrollment events. Expanded Coverage for Women's Preventive Care Under the Affordable Care Act, Baylor University provides female plan participants with expanded access to recommended in-network preventive services without cost sharing. Family and Medical Leave Act Baylor University faculty and staff are eligible for Family and Medical Leave Act (FMLA) leave if they have been employed for at least twelve (12) months, and have worked at least 1,250 hours during the previous twelve (12) month period. HIPAA and Other Federal Law Notices The Health Insurance Portability and Accountability Act and other Federal laws requires an annual notification about important provisions for the UMR/United Healthcare medical plan. HIPAA Notice of Privacy Practices A copy of the notice of privacy practices is available at any time, upon request. HHS.gov Newborns' and Mothers' Health Protection Act Group health plans and health insurance issuers generally may not, under Federal law, restrict benefits for any hospital length of stay in connection with childbirth for the mother or newborn child. Notice of Coverage Options (Marketplace Notice) Notice of ACA Marketplace General Notice of Continuation of Coverage As part of the Affordable Care Act, employers are required to provide faculty and staff a notice of the availability of a Health Insurance Marketplace (also called an Exchange) where individuals may purchase health insurance. www.healthcare.gov UMR/United Healthcare ACA webpage USERRA Rights as an Employee Learn more about the Uniformed Services Employment and Reemployment Rights Act. Baylor Human Resources Putting People First. Clifton Robinson Tower | Suite 200 700 S University Parks Dr Waco, TX 76706 One Bear Place #97053 Waco, TX 76798 askhr@baylor.edu 254-710-2000 Ask HR About Jobs Disclosures Vis