Hybrid/Remote Work Resources Office of the Provost Baylor Round Table Ignite Great Colleges to Work For® Survey Human Resources Careers & Opportunities New Faculty and Staff Steps for New Faculty New Faculty Orientation Research & Learn Apply & Interview New Faculty and Staff Welcome & Orientation Steps for New Faculty New Faculty Orientation Steps for New Staff New Employee Forms Employment Forms by State Transition & Exit Contingent Workers (Auxiliaries) Other Campus Employment Visa Sponsorship and Support Additional Resources New Faculty Orientation New Faculty Orientation is a two-day program focusing on teaching and scholarship within the context of a Christian university. You will meet other Baylor family members - fellow newcomers, professors, administrators, and staff - while learning more about what makes Baylor a great college to work for. The program is is held the Monday and Tuesday of the week prior to the start of the semester and you will receive an email from the Provost's Office with details and logistical information. Academic and campus leaders also attend the sessions, providing you a great opportunity to network and initiate cross-departmental relationships with colleagues. Additionally, you will receive a packet of information including resources across campus, a course catalog, and a notebook. Sample Orientation Sessions Faith and Learning at Baylor Research Opportunities Teaching at Baylor Enhancing the Teaching Role Baylor Information Technology Services Baylor Students Policies and Procedures-FERPA, Legal Requirements Baylor Traditions Baylor Libraries-opportunity to meet departmental liaisons Baylor Human Resources Putting People First. Clifton Robinson Tower | Suite 200 700 S University Parks Dr Waco, TX 76706 One Bear Place #97053 Waco, TX 76798 askhr@baylor.edu 254-710-2000 Ask HR About Jobs Disclosures Visit Policies Human Resources Careers & Opportunities New Faculty and Staff Steps for New Faculty New Faculty Orientation About Career